__children["Backdrop"]["title"].setValue( 'Example: Light Linking Basics (Arnold)' )
__children["Backdrop"]["description"].setValue( 'This example contains the various permutations of light linking on objects:\n\n1. No link (default)\n2. Link to a light\'s location\n3. Link to a set containing a light\n4. Link to a set and the "defaultLights" set\n5. Link to a non-default light\n6. Link to a blank expression\n\nThe main lights and objects come from two distinct streams: the spheres on the left half of the graph, and the lights on the right half. This is done to illustrate the separation of lights and objects in light linking, and provide a scene closer to one that would be used in a light rig.\n\nThe spheres are floating above a plane, and receive rays from any lights that have the Default Light plug checked. Any other additional light they receive is specified by various linking arrangements.\n\nTo view the scene:\n\n1. Select the InteractiveRender node.\n2.In the Node Editor, click play.\n2. Select the Catalogue node.' )
__children["Backdrop"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -5.73694611, -39.784256 ), imath.V2f( 38.1527443, 10 ) ) )
__children["Backdrop"]["__uiPosition"].setValue( imath.V2f( -10.4412212, 139.839432 ) )
__children["Backdrop1"]["title"].setValue( 'Sphere #1: No link' )
__children["Backdrop1"]["description"].setValue( 'No linking is established. The sphere receives light from all lights that belong to the "defaultLights" set.' )
__children["Backdrop1"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -30, -20 ), imath.V2f( 10, 30 ) ) )
__children["Backdrop1"]["__uiPosition"].setValue( imath.V2f( -92.0852356, 52.1903954 ) )
__children["Backdrop2"]["title"].setValue( 'Sphere #2: Link to location' )
__children["Backdrop2"]["description"].setValue( "The sphere is linked to the location of spotlight2, which exists in a parallel stream. When this stream and that stream meet, the link will be made valid.\n\nNotice how the link location is a full path that anticipates the scene hierarchy as it exists at the downstream InteractiveRender node. If the path only reflected the hierarchy from the StandardAttribute2 node's context, Arnold would try and resolve the wrong link location." )
__children["Backdrop2"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -30, -20 ), imath.V2f( 10, 30 ) ) )
__children["Backdrop2"]["__uiPosition"].setValue( imath.V2f( -50.2635422, 52.1622276 ) )
__children["Backdrop3"]["title"].setValue( 'Sphere #3: Link to set' )
__children["Backdrop3"]["description"].setValue( 'The sphere is linked to the "lights:blue" set, which spotlight3 belongs to.\n' )
__children["Backdrop3"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -30, -20 ), imath.V2f( 10, 30 ) ) )
__children["Backdrop3"]["__uiPosition"].setValue( imath.V2f( -8.83079338, 52.1060333 ) )
__children["Backdrop4"]["title"].setValue( 'Sphere #4: Link to set + defaultLights' )
__children["Backdrop4"]["description"].setValue( 'The sphere links to both "lights:yellow" and "defaultLights" sets, so it will be illuminated by both spotlight4 and all lights that have the Default Light plug checked.' )
__children["Backdrop4"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -35, -20 ), imath.V2f( 10, 30 ) ) )
__children["Backdrop4"]["__uiPosition"].setValue( imath.V2f( 37.7097893, 52.1190491 ) )
__children["Backdrop5"]["title"].setValue( 'Sphere #5: Link to non-default light' )
__children["Backdrop5"]["description"].setValue( 'The sphere links to spotlight5, which has its Default Light plug unchecked. Therefore, the sphere and spotlight5 are exclusively linked: spotlight5 is the only source of illumination for this sphere, and the sphere is the only object that receives light from spotlight5.' )
__children["Backdrop5"]["__uiBound"].setValue( imath.Box2f( imath.V2f( -35, -20 ), imath.V2f( 10, 30 ) ) )
